fact WorkItem(id: "WI-208", description: some(value: "Data-flow discharge for acyclic_cell on operation bodies. Per docs/design/cell-runtime.md §'Discharge by data-flow on operation bodies'. Generalizes WI-207's static walk (which rejects sorts with type-graph cycles like dll(prev: Cell[dll], next: Cell[dll], data: E)) by proving the operation set preserves acyclicity at runtime — without runtime cost. Per-Cell.set local rule: for each pointer field f in the value v written to cell c, classify v.f as fresh (just allocated, no incoming references), unchanged (= c.prior.f), or downstream (reachable from c via f-pointers in the prior heap). A Cell.set discharges if every pointer field is fresh/unchanged/downstream. An operation discharges if every Cell.set in its body discharges and every Cell.new is unconstrained. Per-field independence: prev-graph and next-graph are checked separately. Implementation: data-flow analysis pass over operation IR; tracks per-variable origin (Fresh / Param / Derived) and prior-heap reachability via shape analysis. Coverage: linked-structure operations (push_front/back, prepend, delete, splice), tree builds, hash-map insertion. Out of coverage (deferred to runtime age-ordered cells or proposal 030 proof cache): edge swaps (AVL rotate, graph rewriting, observer self-subscription) — these need either strict age-ordering (separate OrderedCell sort) or paper/SMT proof. Sketch shape analysis: each variable v annotated with reachable-cells via each pointer field f, propagated through Cell.get / pattern destructuring / field access. Tests: dll's push_front/push_back/insert_after/delete all clear; intentional cycle_back is rejected with diagnostic identifying the field that closed the cycle; AVL rotate is correctly identified as needing stronger discharge (test the failure path). The discharge produces a fact acyclic_cell[T = V] that the kernel can rely on at Cell[V] sites without further checking. Acceptance: cargo-test green; the dll example operations type-check under the discharge; cycle_back is rejected."), context: none, acceptance: [ToolPasses(tool: "cargo-test", params: none)], depends_on: some(value: ["WI-207"]), generates: none, requires_capability: none, status: Open)
